What the planner should know:
• **Build and runtime:** the harness confirmed the suite is green at `44a2e21f`. From an empty temp directory, `yoyo -p "Reply with exactly: PONG"` writes exactly `PONG\n` and exits 0.
• **Two issues from the creator today:**
  • **#991:** move yoagent to 0.24.1 and use its new retry filter (`retry_safe_events`) for `-p` output going to a pipe. 0.24.1 is published, and `Cargo.toml already says "0.24", so only the lockfile changes. The filter exists at retry.rs:154 and :323 and wraps the event stream agent.prompt() returns. Adopting it will trip the test at src/prompt.rs:3874`, which counts exactly 15 places that print streamed text; that count will need a deliberate update.
  • **#992:** release now if it's good enough. It's 6 days since v0.1.19, so the 14-day cadence alone wouldn't trigger a release; the issue relaxes only the timing.
• **The changelog blocks #992.** The [Unreleased] section has nothing about the yoagent upgrade (#987), #989, or the recent exit-code fixes. Its last bullet says a `/cd` directory's config "is still not applied". Since Day 218 that's false for the deny list, which is now enforced. It needs rewriting before any release. The version rules point to 0.2.0 because of the new flags.
• **#982 is still live, measured today:** `yoyo def nosuchthing`, `yoyo outline nosuch.rs`, a bare `yoyo run` and `yoyo tree --bogus` all print a failure and exit 0. All of these live in the subcommand dispatch code, which took 4 of the last 8 self-driven changes, so the trajectory says to send this session's self-driven slot elsewhere.
• **#988 (Ctrl-C/cancel audit after the upgrade) is unblocked but unprobed.** A cancelled run is treated as a normal stop (src/prompt_retry.rs:63), so it doesn't use up retries. The other questions in the issue are untested.
• **Evolution runs:** the last 4 succeeded and one is in progress. The CI failure the trajectory shows as live is a single test failure from 6 days ago (`test_aaa_session_budget_set_path_live_end_to_end`). It hasn't shown up in any evolve run since, so I'd treat it as an old flake.

Suggested order: #991, then the #992 release with the changelog rewritten first. If only one fits in the session, do #992, because it ships the security fix (--yes --deny used to run denied commands).
